## Expert Approach — Fixing a Terraform Module

**Step 1: Read before fixing.** Run 'terraform validate' first to identify syntax errors. Then read all comments in the file — they usually describe the logical errors too.

**Step 2: Fix one bug at a time.** Validate after each fix so you know exactly which change resolved which error.

**Step 3: Add the missing resources in dependency order.** Route tables depend on the VPC and subnets existing. Flow Logs depend on the IAM role existing. Add them in the right order.

**Step 4: Test with a plan.** After validate passes, run 'terraform plan' (you'll need AWS credentials). Review the plan output — it shows exactly what will be created/modified/destroyed.

**Example fixed route table (different project data):**
```hcl
resource "aws_route_table" "public" {
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id
  route {
    cidr_block = "0.0.0.0/0"
    gateway_id = aws_internet_gateway.main.id
  }
  tags = {
    Name = "example-prod-public-rt"
    Environment = "prod"
    ManagedBy = "terraform"
  }
}
```

